-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Chase H.Q.
  Publisher   Ocean, 1989
  Version     1.3

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Chase H.Q. (1989)(Ocean)(128K).z80
  MD5         cedb31d5860815ef7e871ee249744de5

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Speed needs a
              2MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one; Orig. pace needs
              a 2MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures are drawn on the Next's own graphics layers, so they keep their
  own colours and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is
  unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Speed (needs a 2MB Next), Orig.
              pace (needs a 2MB Next), chosen on the menu, off by default.
  Speed       Colours on the original Spectrum drawings, chosen with the
              arcade game as a reference: a rebuilt grey Porsche with nine
              steering views and black passengers; coloured traffic, roadside
              objects, fire, barricades, effects and capture faces on all five
              stages; a metal dashboard with red and blue sirens; five
              coloured radio faces and a navy message pane; mountain and city
              skylines; colour kept in the attract demo and game over. Layer 2
              and Next sprites; figures are not converted to hardware sprites.
              Needs a 2MB Next. On the menu: Speed, drawn at the Speed pace;
              Orig. pace, at the original pace. Source: Enhanced colours: Jon
              Attree.
  Orig. pace  The same colours following the original's time update by update,
              within about 3% over whole runs; stretches of 20 updates can
              reach +13% in the heaviest scenes. Needs a 2MB Next. Source:
              Enhanced colours: Jon Attree.

  Pace        slowdown removed (-8.0% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless;
              probe 0x8444, 90 game addresses equal at every update against
              the plain build; stage 1, 4 runs of 800 updates and, with the
              archive POKEs, 2 of 3000)

  Changes     1.0: speed pass: road, scenery and screen copy drawn at 28 MHz,
              capped at the original quiet-scene pace
              1.1: Enhanced colours on the menu, off by default, for a 2MB
              Next, at the Speed pace or the original pace; Speed now uses the
              Enhanced engine with its colours off and still fits a 1MB Next;
              fixes a crash at the tunnel mouth in Enhanced colours when a
              wall row has no width
              1.2: Orig. pace follows the original's time on each update, not
              one fixed time: quiet scenes were 3 to 5% slow and stretches up
              to 15%; measured figures in the notes replace the old table.
              Speed and Enhanced Speed are unchanged.
              1.3: two interrupt-safe reads of the CPU speed in Enhanced's
              sound and pace checks; play unchanged

  Note        Keys: ENTER options, 5 redefine (tested: SPACE gear, Q
              accelerate, A brake, O left, P right, X quit, H pause, T turbo),
              4 keyboard, SPACE to start. Modes: Speed alone keeps the
              original artwork and is faster on purpose; Enhanced colours
              [Speed] adds the colours at the Speed pace; Enhanced colours
              [Orig. pace] follows the original's time update by update; Speed
              off is your own game. Known issues: time per update against the
              original, JNext, stage 1, same input: Speed whole -8 to -19%;
              Enhanced Speed -6 to -14%; Orig. pace whole -3.0 to +0.3%, quiet
              -3.1 to +1.2%, busy -5.0 to -0.3%, but 20-update stretches reach
              +13.4%: where the colours' drawing alone takes the original's
              time it cannot be paid back. The original's synchronous sound
              effects still stall play for up to about 0.8 s; the Enhanced
              road motion is approximate and frames can tear. Enhanced needs a
              2MB Next. Missing: hardware untested; no full five-stage
              playthrough or ending checked; joystick not checked.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite credits
   2  Infinite time
   3  1Hit to capture
   4  Infinite turbos

  The archive's POKEs for this release. 1Hit to capture and Infinite turbos
  are written to their source copies in bank 3, which the game copies into
  place at its intro.

